From aa605639682ee8338adf9b3fb6e27cd2ab084cf5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peripheral Pretender setup <pp-setup@localhost>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 12:53:23 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] hw/dma: TCC, SDADC and TSENS DMA triggers; level requests at
 enable

The remaining PIC32CM DMA triggers but the DAC's, as PIC32CM MC00
silicon moved them (firmware/hello APP=dmaprobe, checked by dmatrig):

- TCC: OVF pulses "ovf-dma" at each update condition and retrigger;
  MCx pulses "mc-dma"[x] at each compare match, or for a capture
  channel at each capture into CCx (the DMA's CCx read clears MCx).
  As for the TC, the DMAC tells the TCC whether a channel waits
  ("ovf-dma-wanted", "mc-dma-wanted"), so that it only then steps
  through every event. The SoC wires DMAC_ID_OVF and DMAC_ID_MCn of
  every instance that has these lines.
- SDADC and TSENS RESRDY are level triggers on INTFLAG, like the
  ADC's; each new result kicks the DMAC.

New mchp_dmac_kick_machine() finds the machine's DMAC once and kicks
it; the ADC uses it instead of its own lookup. The U2223 DMAC now
serves a level request already set when a channel is enabled at once
(silicon moved an unread SDADC result within 5 us); it used to wait
for its 20 us batch.

qtest pic32cm-dmac-test: TCC OVF, compare and capture, TSENS, SDADC,
a level request at enable.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
